WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.327
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Advanced.

2
00:00:05.627 --> 00:00:08.886
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.186 --> 00:00:17.388
Unit fifty-one: Mental Health in Society. In this unit, you will discuss mental health with understanding and accuracy.

4
00:00:18.383 --> 00:00:19.907
mental health stigma.

5
00:00:20.607 --> 00:00:25.288
mental health stigma means negative attitudes that make people ashamed to seek help.

6
00:00:25.588 --> 00:00:29.120
Mental health stigma stops many people from talking.

7
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.413
Your turn. Say: mental health stigma.

8
00:00:36.113 --> 00:00:37.660
mental health stigma.

9
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.487
psychological resilience.

10
00:00:41.187 --> 00:00:46.054
psychological resilience means the ability to cope with and recover from difficulties.

11
00:00:46.354 --> 00:00:49.677
Supportive friendships build psychological resilience.

12
00:00:50.377 --> 00:00:53.854
Your turn. Say: psychological resilience.

13
00:00:56.554 --> 00:00:58.542
psychological resilience.

14
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:01.166
anxiety disorder.

15
00:01:01.866 --> 00:01:07.186
anxiety disorder means a condition causing strong, persistent worry or fear.

16
00:01:07.486 --> 00:01:10.090
Anxiety disorders are common and treatable.

17
00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:14.475
Your turn. Say: anxiety disorder.

18
00:01:17.175 --> 00:01:18.664
anxiety disorder.

19
00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:20.628
depression.

20
00:01:21.328 --> 00:01:26.125
depression means a medical condition causing long-lasting low mood.

21
00:01:26.425 --> 00:01:28.924
Depression is an illness, not a weakness.

22
00:01:29.624 --> 00:01:31.986
Your turn. Say: depression.

23
00:01:34.686 --> 00:01:35.641
depression.

24
00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.115
therapy access.

25
00:01:38.815 --> 00:01:43.450
therapy access means the ability to reach professional psychological support.

26
00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:47.085
Therapy access is limited in many rural areas.

27
00:01:47.785 --> 00:01:50.925
Your turn. Say: therapy access.

28
00:01:53.625 --> 00:01:55.195
therapy access.

29
00:01:56.183 --> 00:01:57.266
peer support.

30
00:01:57.966 --> 00:02:02.020
peer support means help from people with similar experiences.

31
00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.771
Peer support groups help students feel less alone.

32
00:02:06.471 --> 00:02:09.123
Your turn. Say: peer support.

33
00:02:11.823 --> 00:02:12.952
peer support.

34
00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:15.323
burnout culture.

35
00:02:16.023 --> 00:02:20.367
burnout culture means a work or study culture that encourages overwork.

36
00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:23.677
Burnout culture treats exhaustion as normal.

37
00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:27.540
Your turn. Say: burnout culture.

38
00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.369
burnout culture.

39
00:02:32.383 --> 00:02:34.116
emotional regulation.

40
00:02:34.816 --> 00:02:39.950
emotional regulation means the ability to manage and respond to emotions.

41
00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.689
Breathing exercises can improve emotional regulation.

42
00:02:44.389 --> 00:02:47.738
Your turn. Say: emotional regulation.

43
00:02:50.438 --> 00:02:52.113
emotional regulation.

44
00:02:53.117 --> 00:02:55.465
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:55.765 --> 00:03:00.074
Rithy, do students at your university talk openly about mental health?

46
00:03:01.383 --> 00:03:04.474
More than before, but the stigma is still strong.

47
00:03:05.783 --> 00:03:07.318
Why do you think that is?

48
00:03:08.617 --> 00:03:14.218
The fear of being judged. Many people see depression as weakness rather than an illness.

49
00:03:15.517 --> 00:03:20.514
That perception is changing, fortunately. Is therapy access improving?

50
00:03:21.817 --> 00:03:25.920
Slowly. Our university has introduced a peer support programme.

51
00:03:27.217 --> 00:03:31.541
Excellent. The reduction of stigma begins with conversations like these.

52
00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:37.557
And with the rejection of burnout culture. Rest is not laziness.

53
00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:42.487
Grammar focus: Nominalisation (mastery).

54
00:03:42.787 --> 00:03:46.632
Nominalisation helps discuss sensitive topics objectively.

55
00:03:46.932 --> 00:03:51.070
The fear of being judged stops people. That perception is changing.

56
00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:54.032
The reduction of stigma begins with conversation.

57
00:03:54.332 --> 00:03:59.443
Nominalisation allows you to discuss sensitive topics in a measured, objective tone.

58
00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:04.043
Now read and listen. Talking About Mental Health.

59
00:04:04.343 --> 00:04:08.931
Mental health conditions affect roughly one in eight people worldwide.

60
00:04:10.217 --> 00:04:14.991
Anxiety disorders and depression are among the most common, and both are treatable.

61
00:04:16.283 --> 00:04:20.640
Yet the fear of being judged prevents many people from seeking help.

62
00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:28.234
In many communities, therapy access is limited by cost, distance and a shortage of professionals.

63
00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:34.417
Peer support programmes have shown promising results, especially among young people.

64
00:04:35.717 --> 00:04:42.116
The promotion of emotional regulation skills in schools may also strengthen psychological resilience.

65
00:04:43.417 --> 00:04:48.655
Experts warn that burnout culture, which glorifies overwork, can damage wellbeing.

66
00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:54.782
Anyone who is struggling is encouraged to talk to someone they trust or to a health professional.

67
00:04:56.083 --> 00:04:58.829
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:04:59.129 --> 00:05:02.208
Help from people with similar experiences is blank.

69
00:05:02.508 --> 00:05:08.065
A, peer support. B, therapy access. C, burnout culture.

70
00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:14.491
The answer is A: peer support.

71
00:05:15.983 --> 00:05:18.122
The noun form of 'reduce' is blank.

72
00:05:18.422 --> 00:05:23.480
A, reducing. B, reduction. C, reducement.

73
00:05:27.483 --> 00:05:29.912
The answer is B: reduction.

74
00:05:31.417 --> 00:05:35.590
'People fear being judged.' → 'The blank of being judged...'

75
00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:39.439
A, fear. B, fearing. C, fearful.

76
00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:46.146
The answer is A: fear.

77
00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:51.240
The ability to cope with and recover from difficulties is blank.

78
00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:57.074
A, psychological resilience. B, anxiety disorder. C, stigma.

79
00:06:01.083 --> 00:06:04.441
The answer is A: psychological resilience.

80
00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:11.328
According to the text, what does the text encourage people who are struggling to do?

81
00:06:11.628 --> 00:06:17.708
A, stay silent. B, talk to someone they trust or a professional. C, work harder.

82
00:06:21.717 --> 00:06:25.841
The answer is B: talk to someone they trust or a professional.

83
00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:34.751
Now it's your turn. Part one: How can schools and universities better support students' mental health?

84
00:06:40.051 --> 00:06:46.265
Part two: Use nominalisation: propose two measures and explain their benefits.

85
00:06:52.565 --> 00:07:04.366
The introduction of peer support groups and the training of teachers to recognise warning signs would make a real difference. Their main benefit would be the reduction of stigma and earlier access to help.

86
00:07:04.666 --> 00:07:07.362
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:13.301
Great work today! You learned eight new words and nominalisation (mastery).

88
00:07:13.601 --> 00:07:17.438
Today's value is empathy. Think about how others feel.

89
00:07:17.738 --> 00:07:20.715
See you in Unit fifty-two. Goodbye!

90
00:07:21.015 --> 00:07:23.830
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

